      "writtenOn": "2026-08-12T22:17:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "isn\u0027t there a race here where once CPU might have entered when !in_nmi (acquires task_lock) and another enters in_nmi (acquires alloc lock) so there is no serialization?",
      "revId": "d3eaf6e16b4380fc317e5fd8f1ecf13d301311bb",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "bc94e369_b9ed596a",
        "filename": "mm/oom_kill.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 142,
      "author": {
        "id": 1004907
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-08-12T22:28:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t think so? Essentially a task that\u0027s in NMI won\u0027t get the lock and won\u0027t look at this thread\u0027s \"-\u003emm\". If we don\u0027t find any \"-\u003emm\" then we\u0027ll return NULL and we\u0027ll skip dumping this particular task. That\u0027s OK.\n\nEssentially:\n* If we return a task with a MM, the lock for that task is held.\n* If we return NULL, no lock is held and the calling function will just return.\n\nDoes that make sense?",
      "parentUuid": "9d3f2726_fea8083d",
      "revId": "d3eaf6e16b4380fc317e5fd8f1ecf13d301311bb",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "68bda30d_1d09e8fb",
        "filename": "mm/oom_kill.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 142,
      "author": {
        "id": 1069543
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-08-13T23:03:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If \"a task that\u0027s in NMI won\u0027t get the lock\", why do we bother to try? Should the code just be this?\n```\nif (in_nmi())\n   continue;\nelse\n   task_lock(t);\n```\nthen we know for sure that it won\u0027t look at this thread\u0027s \"-\u003emm\".",
      "parentUuid": "bc94e369_b9ed596a",
      "revId": "d3eaf6e16b4380fc317e5fd8f1ecf13d301311bb",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4b450e42_28dad260",
        "filename": "mm/oom_kill.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 142,
      "author": {
        "id": 1004907
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-08-13T23:19:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t think so. If I\u0027m reading it right, the whole `dump_tasks()` that we\u0027re calling would be a complete noop if called at NMI time, wouldn\u0027t it? The `dump_tasks()` function walks through all tasks and calls `dump_task()`. If `dump_task()` can\u0027t find a \"MM\" then it just returns without doing anything.\n\nThe idea is that we want to dump the \"MM\" info of all tasks we can. If a specific MM is locked then we can\u0027t safely dump the info, but that doesn\u0027t mean we shouldn\u0027t try to dump the rest.",
      "parentUuid": "68bda30d_1d09e8fb",
      "revId": "d3eaf6e16b4380fc317e5fd8f1ecf13d301311bb",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
