      "side": 1,
      "message": "If spin_trylock() succeeds above and t-\u003emm \u003d\u003d NULL, then doesn\u0027t this need to be spin_unlock(\u0026t-\u003ealloc_lock) for the in_nmi case?\n\nIf this is impossible, then I think a comment is needed to explain why.",
      "revId": "d3eaf6e16b4380fc317e5fd8f1ecf13d301311bb",
