      "writtenOn": "2026-08-13T23:19:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The implementation of `task_unlock()` is:\n\n```\nstatic inline void task_unlock(struct task_struct *p)\n\t__releases(\u0026p-\u003ealloc_lock)\n{\n\tspin_unlock(\u0026p-\u003ealloc_lock);\n}\n```\n\nThe problem is that `include/linux/sched/task.h` doesn\u0027t have a `task_trylock`, so Mayank had to open-code it. \n\nMaybe Mayank could add a comment next to his `spin_trylock` explaining this?",
      "parentUuid": "2121bc66_575e2622",
      "revId": "d3eaf6e16b4380fc317e5fd8f1ecf13d301311bb",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
